### 4.3 How much evidence, and the MDE

Independent observations are round trips, not weeks: N100 ÷ MC100 35 round trips over 1037 weeks, N100 ÷ SC100 36 round trips over 1037 weeks, N100 ÷ Micro250 7 round trips over 201 weeks, MC100 ÷ SC100 43 round trips over 1037 weeks, MC100 ÷ Micro250 9 round trips over 201 weeks, SC100 ÷ Micro250 6 round trips over 201 weeks.

Next to every FAIL above, the smallest edge the test could have seen (2.8 × the null's sd of CAGR): N100 ÷ MC100 undetectable below 2.5 pp a year, N100 ÷ SC100 undetectable below 4.5 pp a year, N100 ÷ Micro250 undetectable below 11.4 pp a year, MC100 ÷ SC100 undetectable below 2.7 pp a year, MC100 ÷ Micro250 undetectable below 8.3 pp a year, SC100 ÷ Micro250 undetectable below 4.3 pp a year. A FAIL means 'too small to see', not 'nothing there'.

